paper-to-pipeline patch for Lua 5.4.9, applied by
scripts/build_gem5_workloads.sh with "patch -p1" in a fresh copy of the
source.

src/lmathlib.c: math.random starts from a fixed seed. Upstream seeds it at
startup from time(NULL) and the address of the Lua state. Under gem5,
time(NULL) returns simulated time, which moves when the predictor changes.
The bundled scripts never call math.random, but a script added later must
not pick up that dependence by accident.

Lua 5.4.9 reads the clock in two more places. Both are hooks that Lua lets
a build override, so the build script sets them with -D instead of
patching.
  luai_makeseed(L)     the string hash seed (src/lstate.c)
  l_randomizePivot()   the table.sort pivot salt (src/ltablib.c)

--- a/src/lmathlib.c
+++ b/src/lmathlib.c
@@ -626,8 +626,10 @@
 ** randomization).
 */
 static void randseed (lua_State *L, RanState *state) {
-  lua_Unsigned seed1 = (lua_Unsigned)time(NULL);
-  lua_Unsigned seed2 = (lua_Unsigned)(size_t)L;
+  /* paper-to-pipeline: a fixed seed. Upstream mixes in time(NULL) and the
+  ** address of 'L', and gem5 answers time(NULL) with simulated time. */
+  lua_Unsigned seed1 = (lua_Unsigned)0x2545F4914F6CDD1Du;
+  lua_Unsigned seed2 = 0;
   setseed(L, state->s, seed1, seed2);
 }
 
